<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia central bank to offer bilateral papers.</title>
<headline>Indonesia central bank to offer bilateral papers.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's central bank, Bank Indonesia, said on Thursday it will offer bilateral central bank papers (SBIs) to drain excess liquidity.</p>
<p>The bank said it will offer one-to-four day SBIs at six percent, one-week at 6.5 percent, two-week at 8.5 percent, one-month at 10.25 percent and three-month at 11.25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
